<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>System Architecture & Participant Tracking | Living Lab Portal</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary: #10b981;
            --primary-dark: #059669;
            --bg-dark: #0f172a;
            --card-bg: #1e293b;
            --text-light: #f8fafc;
            --text-muted: #cbd5e1;
            --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        }

        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-dark);
            color: var(--text-light);
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 40px auto;
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 16px;
            padding: 40px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        }

        .header {
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
            padding-bottom: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        .header h1 {
            color: #4ade80;
            margin: 0 0 10px 0;
            font-size: 2rem;
        }

        .header p {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #38bdf8;
            font-size: 1.4rem;
            margin-top: 35px;
            border-left: 4px solid #38bdf8;
            padding-left: 12px;
        }

        h3 {
            color: #f8fafc;
            font-size: 1.15rem;
            margin-top: 25px;
        }

        .card-box {
            background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 22px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        /* Audience Tabs Styling */
        .tab-buttons {
            display: flex;
            gap: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
        }

        .tab-btn {
            background: #334155;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 18px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: 600;
            transition: all 0.2s ease;
        }

        .tab-btn.active {
            background: var(--primary);
            color: white;
        }

        .tab-content {
            display: none;
        }

        .tab-content.active {
            display: block;
        }

        ul {
            padding-left: 20px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        li strong {
            color: var(--text-light);
        }

        .back-nav {
            margin-top: 40px;
            padding-top: 20px;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
        }

        .btn-back {
            background: #334155;
            color: var(--text-light);
            text-decoration: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-weight: 600;
            transition: background 0.2s;
        }

        .btn-back:hover {
            background: #475569;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- HEADER -->
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Platform Mechanics & Portfolio Tracking</h1>
            <p>An inside look at how the living lab system logs participant progression, manages data telemetry, and bridges real-time needs with institutional solutions.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 1: AUDIENCE TRANSLATIONS -->
        <h2>1. Explaining the System by Audience</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 20px;">Select an audience below to see how the system's core capabilities are tailored:</p>
        
        <div class="tab-buttons">
            <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="openTab(event, 'grant')">Grant Committee</button>
            <button class="tab-btn" onclick="openTab(event, 'tech')">Tech-Savvy Partner</button>
            <button class="tab-btn" onclick="openTab(event, 'layman')">Complete Layman</button>
       
        </div>
       
        <!-- Grant View -->
        <div id="grant" class="tab-content active card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #38bdf8;">Impact, Scalability, &amp; Institutional Accountability</h3>
            <p>The platform provides a robust, verifiable framework for participatory research, resource optimization, and institutional data sharing:</p>
            <ul>
             <li><strong>Benefit Modeling:</strong> Translating raw metrics into quantified outcomes (carbon offset, water efficiency, yield gains).</li>
                <li><strong>Needs-to-Solutions Routing:</strong> Cross-referencing identified deficits (nitrogen depletion, equipment gaps) against a curated database of verified interventions and extension partner solutions.</li>
            </ul>
        </div> 
                
    
        <!-- Tech View -->
        <div id="tech" class="tab-content card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #38bdf8;">Architecture, Pipelines, &amp; Feedback Loops</h3>
            <p>The system operates as an end-to-end, schema-driven telemetry and matching platform. On the collection side, field agents or IoT sensors log standardized data points into structured JSON/CSV schemas with strict UTC timestamps and metadata validation to prevent data drift or anomalous skew.</p>
            <p>Once ingested, the engine runs a multi-factor vector or rule-based matching algorithm indexing incoming field conditions against two dynamic matrices:</p>
            <ul>
             
         </li><strong>Rigorous Data Collection:</strong> Enforces strict metadata standards, calibration protocols, and chain-of-custody tracking so community-contributed field telemetry is clean and ready for academic extension databases.</li>
                <li><strong>Dynamic Benefit Realization:</strong> Translates field metrics into clear impact indicators, providing transparent tracking for ESG reporting and grant KPI compliance.</li>
                <li><strong>Targeted Needs Alignment:</strong> Bridges the gap between field-level challenges and evidence-based interventions, ensuring funding and resources deploy where they yield the highest marginal impact.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <!-- Layman View -->
        <div id="layman" class="tab-content card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #38bdf8;">The Smart Health Tracker Analogy</h3>
            <p>Think of it like a smart health tracker for a farm or community project, but instead of counting steps, it looks after the health of the land and project:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>How we collect data:</strong> People out in the field use a simple tool to record conditions—like checking soil moisture or noting when supplies run low.</li>
                <li><strong>How it matches benefits:</strong> The system automatically looks at those notes and says, <em>"Because your moisture levels are improving, you're on track to save water and qualify for this benefit."</em></li>
                <li><strong>How it connects solutions:</strong> If the system spots a problem—like a nutrient shortage—it digs through a digital library of expert advice to suggest the exact fix right when you need it.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2: PARTICIPANT PROGRESSION & PORTFOLIO -->
        <h2>2. Participant Progression &amp; Portfolio Building</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">How participants are tracked from the waitlist through program completion:</p>

        <div class="card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 1: Waitlist &amp; Initial Profiling</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong>What they do:</strong> Complete initial intake, baseline survey, and orientation modules.</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;"><strong>Portfolio Impact:</strong> Establishes baseline benchmarks, places participants in appropriate tiers, and logs initial coordinator engagement.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 2: Active Module Progression</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong>What they do:</strong> Complete interactive training modules (like Module 203) and pass case study quizzes.</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;"><strong>Portfolio Impact:</strong> Automatically populates a verifiable transcript of acquired competencies (e.g., telemetry certified, safety protocol trained) backed by earned XP.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 3: Field Contribution &amp; Telemetry Logging</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong>What they do:</strong> Conduct real-world field work—logging soil samples, reporting environmental conditions, or tracking labor hours.</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;"><strong>Portfolio Impact:</strong> Proves hands-on execution, turning theoretical learning into a trackable record of contributions to academic extension partners.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-box">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 4: Crisis Resolution &amp; Resource Utilization</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 5px;"><strong>What they do:</strong> Respond to system alerts, resolve environmental deficits, or request/offer shared resources.</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;"><strong>Portfolio Impact:</strong> Highlights problem-solving capability and community leadership, vital for securing advanced grants.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3: SYSTEM FEATURES -->
        <h2>3. Core System Features Enabling Tracking &amp; Matching</h2>
        <div class="card-box">
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Structured JSON/CSV Telemetry Schemas:</strong> Ensures every user action and field data point is stored with strict metadata (UTC timestamps, plot IDs) for data cleanliness.</li>
                <li><strong>Dynamic Relational Database Mapping:</strong> Connects Participant Profiles (skills, geographic radius, labor availability) directly against Opportunity/Need Nodes (grants, crisis alerts, labor shortages).</li>
                <li><strong>Automated Triage &amp; Trigger Engine:</strong> Scans incoming telemetry in real-time, instantly evaluating active participants to initiate emergency or resource matches when thresholds are crossed.</li>
                <li><strong>Gamified XP &amp; Milestone Ledger:</strong> Logs progress points and module states securely, serving as an objective trust metric for matching high-stakes grants or leadership roles.</li>
                <li><strong>Automated Portfolio Synthesis:</strong> Aggregates verified data logs, completed modules, and field contributions into a portable, exportable impact report ready for grant committees.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- FOOTER NAV -->
        <div class="back-nav">
            <a href="index.html" class="btn-back">← Return to Home Hub</a>
            <span style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">System Version 2.1</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function openTab(evt, tabName) {
            const contents = document.getElementsByClassName("tab-content");
            for (let i = 0; i < contents.length; i++) {
                contents[i].classList.remove("active");
            }
            
            const buttons = document.getElementsByClassName("tab-btn");
            for (let i = 0; i < buttons.length; i++) {
                buttons[i].classList.remove("active");
            }
            
            document.getElementById(tabName).classList.add("active");
            evt.currentTarget.classList.add("active");
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
